       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is about 5 times the usual maximum metformin dose. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Common metformin doses per administration are:\n- **425 mg**, which isn't a standard strength.\n- **500 mg** three times daily (1,500 mg/day).\n- **850 mg** three times daily (2,550 mg/day, the maximum).\n\nWhat dose did you intend? Once you confirm, I'll enter it as oral, three times daily with meals. If you really do want 4250 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly and I'll reconsider. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
