     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 12,750 mg/day of metformin is in the range we treat as an overdose. Acute ingestions above about 5 g can cause severe lactic acidosis, and no indication supports a therapeutic dose that high. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg orally three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or a lower dose if you're titrating up.\n- **Help you reach pharmacy.** If you have a clinical reason I'm missing, a pharmacist or the attending can review it and place the order through their process.\n- **Look at the underlying goal.** If glycemic control is the issue, I can enter a different or additional agent that you choose.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
